Subject: wined3d: upload fixed-function texture matrices only for fixed-function draws
Date: 2026-10-18
Applies to: CrossOver 26.3.0 Wine sources, after 0018
Files changed: dlls/wined3d/stateblock.c

wined3d marks the texture matrices changed with every vertex declaration
change, because the fixed-function vertex pipeline reads them according to
the texture coordinate formats. wined3d_device_apply_stateblock() then built
all eight matrices and uploaded them. BO1 changes vertex declarations about
10,000 times per second with a vertex shader bound, which never reads them:
about 35 ms per second of the game's thread. While a vertex shader is bound,
the change is now only remembered, and the matrices are uploaded with the
next draw that uses the fixed-function vertex pipeline.

Test: tools/d3d9-texmatrix-test.c (a matrix set while a vertex shader is
bound applies to the next fixed-function draw), and the other
tools/d3d9-*-test.c
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, like the Wine files it modifies.
---
--- a/dlls/wined3d/stateblock.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/stateblock.c
@@ -87,6 +87,9 @@
     enum wined3d_stateblock_type type;
 
     struct wined3d_saved_states changed;
+    /* Texture matrices changed while a vertex shader was bound; uploaded with
+     * the next draw that uses the fixed-function vertex pipeline. */
+    bool texture_matrices_pending;
 
     struct wined3d_stateblock_state stateblock_state;
     struct wined3d_light_state light_state;
@@ -3959,10 +3962,21 @@
         }
     }
 
-    if (changed->texture_matrices)
+    /* Texture matrices feed only the fixed-function vertex pipeline, but they
+     * are marked changed with every vertex declaration change, which games
+     * can do thousands of times per second with a vertex shader bound. While
+     * a vertex shader is bound, only remember the change, and build and
+     * upload the eight matrices for the next draw without a vertex shader,
+     * the only kind that reads them. */
+    if (changed->texture_matrices && state->vs)
     {
+        stateblock->texture_matrices_pending = true;
+    }
+    else if (changed->texture_matrices || (stateblock->texture_matrices_pending && !state->vs))
+    {
         struct wined3d_ffp_vs_constants constants;
 
+        stateblock->texture_matrices_pending = false;
         for (i = 0; i < WINED3D_MAX_FFP_TEXTURES; ++i)
             get_texture_matrix(state, i, &constants.texture_matrices[i]);
         wined3d_device_context_push_constants(context,
